  "about": "What have I accomplished?\n\nI currently work as Software Development Engineer at Microsoft headquarter in Redmond, WA.  I am in the seller platform services team under windows 10, in which I play an important role as UX developer.  During my career at Microsoft, I have delivered tangible improvement, such as the recent website project that I implemented from scratch successfully delivers rich UI experience and high performance using Single Page App framework, along with other modernized server-side technologies and infrastructure that greatly improves work productivity and site stability.  In addition to my expertise in front-end UX, I am responsible and would love to continue to work for full-stack development that involves middle-tier web services development, deployment/performance monitoring, cloud services, and web test framework.  Thank to my experience in UX test team in my first year at Microsoft, I am a developer with tester mind set, and always keep web test automation and E2E testing as priority in my development activities.\n\nSkills\n\nLanguages: C#, Java, C++, Visual Basic\t \nOS: Window server 2012, Linux, windows phone 8 \nDB/Storage: MS SQL Server 2012, Azure Cloud Storage, T-SQL, SSRS\t \nFrameworks: .NET framework 4.5, Single Page App framework \nWeb Technologies (Server-Side): ASP.NET MVC5, Web API2, WCF, RESTful service, Window Service, Windows Workflow, IIS \nWeb Technologies (Client-Side): AJAX, Javascript, JS libraries (JQuery, KnockoutJS, DurandalJS, D3JS, RequireJS, etc), HTML5, CSS \nTest\t: web testing, UX test automation frameworks and monitoring tools (Selenium, Gomez) \nGraphics/GUI: XMAL, Java Swing, OpenGL\n\nWhat I am looking for\n\nI am looking for the next place I can apply my expertise and contribute in Los Angeles area, as I am determined to relocate to LA.  I am passionate to take my client-side skills to the next level so I would love to work in an environment where open source and modernization of current platform is encouraged.",
